; Regression test for issue #3327: a report that sums postings, as -M does,
; books the same unrealized gain as one that does not — under the footing of
; #3344, the gain the grouped report books is the one its subtotals can
; carry: the realized part in Income:Gains, with the unrealized remainder
; left unbooked, since the subtotals carry no cost to measure it from
; (see the note beside the -M block).
;
; Summed by month, the postings to Assets:Broker become one posting of
; several commodities, which keeps the lots but not their costs, so each lot
; is measured from its lot price instead.  ABC rose from $10 to $30, and
; selling 5 of the 10 ABC realized $100 of the gain, which leaves $100
; unrealized on the 5 still held.

2024-01-01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 ABC @ $10.00
    Assets:Broker

P 2024-03-01 ABC $30.00

2024-04-01 Sell
    Assets:Broker   -5 ABC {$10.00} @ $30.00
    Assets:Broker    $150.00
    Income:Gains

test bal -V --unrealized --now 2024/06/01
             $200.00  Assets:Broker
            $-100.00  Equity:Unrealized Gains
            $-100.00  Income:Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test

; Since #3344 a report that groups postings by period, weekday or payee
; passes on subtotals that carry no cost, and keeps the revaluation between
; postings instead of booking from basis, which would count the $100.00
; realized by the sale a second time (regress/unrealized-grouped-lot-sale).
; The grouped report shows the realized gain alone and does not foot.
test bal -V --unrealized --now 2024/06/01 -M
             $200.00  Assets:Broker
            $-100.00  Income:Gains
--------------------
             $100.00
end test
